# Testing Rules

## Colocation: always inside `__tests__/`
Test files must live inside a `__tests__/` folder colocated within the same FSD slice/layer directory as the source file. Never place a test file next to the source at the same level.

```text
widgets/person/
  models/
    usePersonModel.ts
    __tests__/
      usePersonModel.test.ts
  ui/
    PersonCard.tsx
    __tests__/
      PersonCard.test.tsx
```

## What to test per layer
| Layer | What to test |
|-------|--------------|
| `shared-app/**/logics` | Pure functions (pagination, mappers) |
| `models/` | Hooks via `@testing-library/react` + provider wrappers |
| `api/` | Thin wrappers — mock `get/post/...` from `@/config/api` |
| `ui/` | Presentational only — render with props, assert roles/labels |

## TanStack Query v5 in tests
```typescript
// ✅ New QueryClient per test, retries disabled
const queryClient = new QueryClient({
  defaultOptions: { queries: { retry: false } },
});

render(
  <QueryClientProvider client={queryClient}>
    <ComponentUnderTest />
  </QueryClientProvider>
);

// ✅ Prefer mocking the API module over real network calls
vi.mock("../api/personApi");
```

## Forbidden
```typescript
// ❌ Testing t() / translation strings inside UI tests — strings come from the model
expect(screen.getByText("مدیریت کاربران")).toBeInTheDocument();

// ❌ Reaching into hook internals instead of testing via rendered output
const { result } = renderHook(() => usePersonModel());
expect(result.current._internalCache).toBeDefined();

// ❌ Test file next to source at the same level
widgets/person/models/usePersonModel.test.ts // must be in __tests__/

// ❌ Real network calls instead of mocking the API module
mutationFn: personApi.create // unmocked in a widget model test
```
